# [[.Title]]

Built with [Coyote](https://github.com/farhapartex/coyote).

## Running it

The first time, create the schema and an account to sign in with:

```
coyote start                              # in one terminal
coyote makemigrations --name=initial      # in another
coyote migrate
coyote createsuperadmin
```

After that, `coyote start` is all you need.

The site is on http://127.0.0.1:8000/ and the admin portal on http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/.

## Layout

```
main.go        routes and mounting
settings.go    configuration; read by everything else
migrations/    generated migrations; commit them
templates/     layouts, partials and pages
static/        css, images, javascript
.env           local values, git-ignored
```

Migrations written by `coyote makemigrations` land in `migrations/`, which `main.go` imports blank
so they register themselves at startup.

## Configuration

`.env` supplies values; `settings.go` decides what they mean. A real environment variable always
wins over the file, so a container can override anything without editing it.
